    title: "Palestinian injured, six others detained during raids in West Bank",
    summary: "Palestinian injured, six others detained during raids in West Bank A Palestinian youth was wounded in the leg by Israeli gunfire during a raid in the Kafr Saba neighbourhood of Qalqilya in the occupied West Bank, Quds News Network reported. Israel’s military said a \"hit was confirmed\" after its forces opened fire in the city of Qalqilya overnight after several Palestinians threw stones at its soldiers. During the raid, Israeli forces also stormed a home belonging to the Shawahneh family and caused damage to its contents, Wafa reported. Six Palestinians, including two brothers, were detained by Israeli forces during raids in Jenin governorate, and the village of Kafr Qalil, south of Nablus, Wafa said. The aftermath after Israeli occupation forces raided and ransacked a Palestinian home in the village of Kafr Qalil, south of Nablus in the occupied West Bank, early this morning. https://t.co/Yfr0hHvfYD — Quds News Network (@QudsNen) November 8, 2026",
    preview: "Palestinian injured, six others detained during raids in West Bank A Palestinian youth was wounded in the leg by Israeli gunfire during a raid in the Kafr Saba neighbourhood of Qalqilya in the occupied West Bank, Quds News Network reported. Israel’s military said a \"hit was confirmed\" after its forces opened fire in the city of Qalqilya overnight after several Palestinians threw stones at its soldiers. During the raid, Israeli forces also stormed a home belonging to the Shawahneh family and caused damage to its contents, Wafa reported.",
    body: "Palestinian injured, six others detained during raids in West Bank A Palestinian youth was wounded in the leg by Israeli gunfire during a raid in the Kafr Saba neighbourhood of Qalqilya in the occupied West Bank, Quds News Network reported. Israel’s military said a \"hit was confirmed\" after its forces opened fire in the city of Qalqilya overnight after several Palestinians threw stones at its soldiers.\n\nDuring the raid, Israeli forces also stormed a home belonging to the Shawahneh family and caused damage to its contents, Wafa reported. Six Palestinians, including two brothers, were detained by Israeli forces during raids in Jenin governorate, and the village of Kafr Qalil, south of Nablus, Wafa said. The aftermath after Israeli occupation forces raided and ransacked a Palestinian home in the village of Kafr Qalil, south of Nablus in the occupied West Bank, early this morning.\n\nhttps://t.co/Yfr0hHvfYD — Quds News Network (@QudsNen) November 8, 2026",
